<title>USA: FCC chairman to announce plans to step down.</title>
<headline>FCC chairman to announce plans to step down.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Communications Commission Chairman Reed Hundt was set to announce later Tuesday his plans to leave the agency, sources close to the FCC said.</p>
<p>Hundt also was expected to ask President Bill Clinton to begin the process of finding a successor for the nation's top communications regulator. Hundt is not expected to leave the FCC immediately, the sources said, and instead is expected to stay on until a new chairman is in place.</p>
</text>
